{"hit_count":329}"}, {"id": "PMID:42848984", "text": "{"id":"PMID:42848984","title":"Astrocytic and Axonal Injury Biomarkers in AQP4 Antibody-Positive NMOSD: Insights From PREVENT and CHAMPION-NMOSD.","year":"2026","journal":"Neurology(R) neuroimmunology & neuroinflammation","abstract":"Background and objectives Glial fibrillary acidic protein (GFAP) and neurofilament light chain (NfL) are biomarkers of astrocytic and axonal injury, respectively, in aquaporin-4 antibody-positive neuromyelitis optica spectrum disorder (AQP4-Ab+ NMOSD). We evaluated serum GFAP and NfL levels during treatment with complement component 5 inhibitors eculizumab or ravulizumab and examined associations between pretreatment biomarker levels, clinical characteristics, and on-trial relapse risk using samples from the PREVENT (eculizumab) and CHAMPION-NMOSD (ravulizumab) phase 3 trials. Methods Serum GFAP and NfL levels were analyzed retrospectively in PREVENT and prospectively in CHAMPION-NMOSD and compared with levels in demographically matched external healthy donors. Associations between baseline clinical characteristics and high biomarker levels (≥2 SDs above the healthy donor mean) were evaluated using logistic regression with a test-and-validate strategy. Changes throughout treatment were assessed relative to pretreatment baseline. Biomarker changes associated with adjudicated on-trial relapses were examined. Associations between baseline biomarker levels and time to first adjudicate…"}
